{"type":"text","text":"Both metasprites are on the sheet and confirmed by `list_sprites` while the emulator was paused, then saved with `record_mapping` (confidence 1) and promoted to the ROM's mapping file (5 sprites now, including the pre-existing small_mario/goomba/block_coin).\n\n## `mushroom` — super mushroom\nWorld 1-1, paused the instant it popped out of the **left ? block of the brick row** (level x≈336; the lone first ? block at x≈256 gives the coin, and the right ? of the row at x≈368 also gives a coin). 4 OAM entries, origin (142,131), a 16×16 metasprite, all **sprite palette 6** (`[$0F,$16,$30,$27]` red cap / white spots / orange shading), all `behind_background`, no flips:\n\n| OAM tile | +x | +y | flip | palette |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `$76` (118) | +0 | +0 | none | 6 |\n| `$77` (119) | +8 | +0 | none | 6 |\n| `$78` (120) | +0 | +8 | none | 6 |\n| `$79` (121) | +8 | +8 | none | 6 |\n\n## `big_mario` — big Mario after eating it\nAfter touching the mushroom (`$0754` 1→0, `$0756` 0→1, score +1000 → 001200), 8 OAM entries, origin (142,177), a 16×32 metasprite (no `$FC` filler — every slot is drawn), all **sprite palette 4** (`[$0F,$16,$27,$18]` red / orange skin / olive), no `behind_background`:\n\n| OAM tile | +x | +y | flip | palette |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `$00` (0) | +0 | +0 | none | 4 |\n| `$01` (1) | +8 | +0 | none | 4 |\n| `$4C` (76) | +0 | +8 | none | 4 |\n| `$4D` (77) | +8 | +8 | none | 4 |\n| `$4A` (74) | +0 | +16 | none | 4 |\n| `$4A` (74) | +8 | +16 | **flip_h** | 4 |\n| `$4B` (75) | +0 | +24 | none | 4 |\n| `$4B` (75) | +8 | +24 | **flip_h** | 4 |\n\nSo big Mario is six distinct CHR tiles with the bottom two rows' right halves mirrored. The 16×32 small-Mario form, by contrast, is the same 16×16 body plus four blank `$FC` fillers above it.\n\nNotes on method: the emulator was actually running the attract demo at first (my inputs did nothing), so I pressed Start twice to start a real game; I then placed small Mario under the mushroom block with RAM writes to player_x (`$006D`/`$0086`) with `$0057`/`$0700` zeroed so he jumped straight up (an earlier un-zeroed jump drifted him into the neighbouring coin block), and finally let the mushroom bounce off the green pipe back into him to grow. Everything was inspected on held frames."}
